@title Real-time quote pricing model architecture
@subtitle ML Platform · Orchard Insurance · reviewed 2026-10-12

# Overview

The service prices about 450 quotes per second at peak, with a p99 target of 250 ms.

# Architecture diagram

diagram ml dir=LR title="Quote pricing"
ml: portal "Agent Portal" user
ml: apigw "API Gateway" lb
ml: model "Model Bucket" store
ml: infer "Inference Lambda" fn
ml: sm "SageMaker Endpoint" svc
ml: cache "Feature Cache" cache
ml: train "Training Pipeline" svc
ml: reg "Model Registry" store
ml: group inf "Inference VPC" infer, sm, cache
ml: group prod "Prod account" apigw, model, inf
ml: group mlacct "ML account" train, reg
ml: portal -> apigw : quote request
ml: apigw -> infer : invoke
ml: infer -> cache : get features
ml: infer -> sm : predict
ml: train -> reg : register model
ml: reg -> model : approved artifact
ml: model -> sm : load model

# Capacity

table = Component,Size,Scaling; SageMaker Endpoint,ml.c6i.2xlarge,4 to 12 instances on invocations per instance; Inference Lambda,1024 MB,200 reserved concurrency; Feature Cache,cache.r7g.large,2 replicas

# Deployment

1. Register the model.
2. Approve it in Model Registry.
3. Blue/green deploy, shifting 10% of traffic every 5 minutes.
4. Roll back automatically if p99 exceeds 250 ms.

!! The Feature Cache is not a source of truth. A cache miss falls back to the policy database and adds about 90 ms.
